@startuml Banking System - System Architecture

title Banking System - System Architecture Diagram

!define RECTANGLE class

' ============= PRESENTATION LAYER =============

package "Presentation Layer" {
    [Web Browser] as browser
    [HTML Pages] as html
    [JavaScript Client] as js
    [CSS Styling] as css
    
    browser --> html
    browser --> js
    browser --> css
}

' ============= API LAYER =============

package "API Layer (Spring Boot)" {
    [Customer Controller] as customerCtrl
    [Account Controller] as accountCtrl
    [Transaction Controller] as txnCtrl
    [Transaction History Controller] as historyCtrl
    [Audit Log Controller] as auditCtrl
    [Settlement Controller] as settlementCtrl
    
    note right of customerCtrl
      REST endpoints:
      - POST /register
      - POST /login
      - PUT /change-password
    end note
}

' ============= SERVICE LAYER =============

package "Service Layer (Business Logic)" {
    [Customer Service] as customerSvc
    [Account Service] as accountSvc
    [Transaction Service] as txnSvc
    [Audit Log Service] as auditSvc
    [Settlement Service] as settlementSvc
    
    note right of txnSvc
      Core banking operations:
      - Deposit/Withdraw/Transfer
      - Transaction limits validation
      - Undo/Redo functionality
      - Daily settlement
    end note
}

' ============= DATA STRUCTURES =============

package "Custom Data Structures" {
    [Transaction Queue] as queue
    [Transaction Stack] as stack
    [Transaction History] as history
    
    note right of history
      Implements Command Pattern:
      - Undo Stack (LIFO)
      - Redo Stack (LIFO)
      - Reversible operations
    end note
}

' ============= REPOSITORY LAYER =============

package "Repository Layer (Data Access)" {
    [Customer Repository] as customerRepo
    [Account Repository] as accountRepo
    [Transaction Repository] as txnRepo
    [Audit Log Repository] as auditRepo
}

' ============= DATABASE LAYER =============

database "MongoDB" {
    [customers] as customerDB
    [accounts] as accountDB
    [transactions] as txnDB
    [audit_logs] as auditDB
}

' ============= UTILITIES =============

package "Utilities & Configuration" {
    [Logging Util] as logging
    [Security Config] as security
    [Web Config (CORS)] as webConfig
    [Mongo Config] as mongoConfig
}

' ============= RELATIONSHIPS =============

' Presentation to API
js --> customerCtrl : HTTP/REST
js --> accountCtrl : HTTP/REST
js --> txnCtrl : HTTP/REST
js --> historyCtrl : HTTP/REST
js --> auditCtrl : HTTP/REST

' API to Service
customerCtrl --> customerSvc
accountCtrl --> accountSvc
txnCtrl --> txnSvc
historyCtrl --> txnSvc
auditCtrl --> auditSvc
settlementCtrl --> settlementSvc

' Service to Service
customerSvc --> auditSvc
accountSvc --> customerSvc
accountSvc --> txnSvc
accountSvc --> auditSvc
txnSvc --> accountSvc
txnSvc --> customerSvc
txnSvc --> auditSvc
settlementSvc --> auditSvc

' Service to Data Structures
txnSvc --> queue : FIFO pending
txnSvc --> stack : LIFO recent
txnSvc --> history : Undo/Redo

' Service to Repository
customerSvc --> customerRepo
accountSvc --> accountRepo
txnSvc --> txnRepo
auditSvc --> auditRepo
settlementSvc --> txnRepo

' Repository to Database
customerRepo --> customerDB
accountRepo --> accountDB
txnRepo --> txnDB
auditRepo --> auditDB

' Utilities
logging ..> txnSvc : logs
logging ..> auditSvc : logs
security ..> customerCtrl : secures
webConfig ..> customerCtrl : CORS
mongoConfig ..> customerRepo : configures

' ============= NOTES =============

note as architecture_notes
**Architecture Highlights:**

**Layered Architecture:**
- Presentation Layer: HTML/CSS/JavaScript
- API Layer: REST Controllers
- Service Layer: Business Logic
- Repository Layer: Data Access
- Database Layer: MongoDB

**Design Patterns:**
- MVC (Model-View-Controller)
- Repository Pattern
- Command Pattern (Undo/Redo)
- Dependency Injection
- Service Layer Pattern

**Key Features:**
- RESTful API design
- CORS enabled for cross-origin
- MongoDB for NoSQL storage
- Custom data structures (Queue, Stack)
- Comprehensive audit logging
- Transaction undo/redo capability
- Automated settlement jobs
end note

note as data_flow
**Data Flow:**

1. User Action → Browser
2. Browser → JavaScript Client
3. JavaScript → REST API (JSON)
4. Controller → Service Layer
5. Service → Repository
6. Repository → MongoDB
7. Response flows back up

**Transaction Flow:**
1. Validate user & account
2. Check transaction limits
3. Process transaction
4. Update balances
5. Log to audit
6. Push to queue/stack
7. Add to undo history
end note

note as security_note
**Security Measures:**

- Password hashing
- Session management
- CORS configuration
- Transaction authentication
- Audit trail for all actions
- Account closure verification
end note

@enduml
